          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "alg7-c4-ex1003-e",
          "part": "e",
          "equation": "(5x+3)^2=5x+3",
          "domain": "x in R; no excluded values.",
          "exact_result": "x in {-3/5,-2/5}",
          "derivation": [
            "Let t=5x+3. Then t^2=t is equivalent to t(t-1)=0.",
            "In x, this is (5x+3)(5x+2)=0.",
            "Thus 5x+3=0 or 5x+3=1, giving x=-3/5 or x=-2/5. Do not divide by 5x+3, since that would discard the first root."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "alg7-c4-ex1003-f",
          "part": "f",
          "equation": "(5x+3)^2=(3x+5)^2",
          "domain": "x in R; no excluded values.",
          "exact_result": "x in {-1,1}",
          "derivation": [
            "The difference of squares is [(5x+3)-(3x+5)][(5x+3)+(3x+5)].",
            "This equals (2x-2)(8x+8)=16(x-1)(x+1).",
            "Consequently x=1 or x=-1. Both sign branches of equal squares have been retained."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "alg7-c4-ex1003-g",
          "part": "g",
          "equation": "(4x+5)^2=4(x+5)^2",
          "domain": "x in R; no excluded values.",
          "exact_result": "x in {-5/2,5/2}",
